<title>FRANCE: Sanofi softens on weak sentiment.</title>
<headline>Sanofi softens on weak sentiment.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French pharmaceuticals firm Sanofi fell 1.61 percent to 549 francs at 1038 GMT, as sentiment turned against the stock which has risen strongly in recent weeks.</p>
<p>Traders cited a report in the Financial Times which said the stock was perhaps too expensive at current market prices to attract potential suitors, especially if parent Elf Aquitaine retained a big stake. The report was a possible trigger for profit-taking, one broker said.</p>
<p>Sanofi has risen strongly since Elf said last month it was ready to cut its majority stake in Sanofi.</p>
</text>
